cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the D'Agnese Chart Operator, the D'Agnese Equidistribution Loss or DIF-FNO, please cite it as below."
title: "The D'Agnese Chart Operator: Certified, Exactly Invertible, Adaptively Learned Charts for Neural Operators"
abstract: >-
  A Fourier neural operator evaluated on a certified chart. The D'Agnese
  triangular chart is a constructive diffeomorphism of the reference square
  built from strictly positive increments, so global injectivity, a positive
  Jacobian determinant (computed as a product of positive factors), a
  closed-form inverse at arbitrary points and the parameter-free bound
  det(J) >= eps^2 > 0 hold for every parameter value. The D'Agnese
  Equidistribution Loss gives the chart a classical objective: it vanishes
  exactly on equidistributing meshes, is scale free, and minimises a certified
  upper bound on the representation error at fixed resolution. The repository
  also keeps the DIF-FNO v1 line (softplus barrier and Lipschitz-certified
  deformation) as the ablation that motivates the construction.
